<title>USA: Motorola introduces lower-cost, high-tech phone.</title>
<headline>Motorola introduces lower-cost, high-tech phone.</headline>
<dateline>LIBERTYVILLE, Ill. 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc, on Monday, introduced a less expensive version of its high-tech StarTAC cellular phone.</p>
<p>The new model, StarTAC 6000, will sell for about $500-$1,000, compared to more than $1,000 for the original StarTAC, said David Pinsky, a spokesman for Motorola's cellular subscribr unit.</p>
<p>The new phone has fewer features, a different battery and weighs 3.6 ounces, compared to 3.1 ounces for the original, Pinsky said.</p>
<p>--Reuters Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
